onal locale override (e.g. “en-US”) to use instead of the device’s language."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"An empty string or "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" uses the device’s language. The value is trimmed and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"canonicalized before use, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"EN\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"en\""},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"En\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are equivalent and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"en_US\""},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"en-US\""},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["    The locale is fixed for the lifetime of the returned instance. Passing a different `locale` for an","    already initialized `channelKey` has no effect - call `Zendesk.invalidate()` first, then `initialize`","    with the new locale.","","    Backend content — bot replies, settings and campaigns — follows this locale, as does the","    UIKit messaging interface (labels, buttons, error messages, VoiceOver descriptions, dates and","    plural forms). Lookup falls back from an exact match (`\"en-AU\"`) to the closest available","    translation (`\"en-GB\"`) and finally to the SDK's built-in English. Your app's own string","    overrides in `Bundle.main` continue to take precedence for the chosen locale.","","    Some things deliberately keep following the device: layout *direction*, Help Center article","    *content*, the Zendesk Voice SDK interface, and regional formatting (calendar, number separators,","    file-size units)."]}],"name":"locale"},{"name":"completionHandler","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A block that takes a "},{"code":"Result","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" enum type. In the case of a success, a "}